+### 2.3 Why the PROCEED cannot be attested
+
+- The finding is expressly **VOID for any other bytes** ("Any pinned byte change voids this
+  finding and requires a fresh audit"). The exact §1 set is not present on canonical main.
+- C1 (fix lands unchanged) is unmet: `e372454a` is not an ancestor of main.
+- C2 (hash inventory/dict/order updated to §1 and `verify-landed` green on main) is unmet:
+  the phase-1 dict still pins the §1 bytes and `verify-landed` is `hold`.
+- C3 requires a source-attested phase PROCEED "itself independently reviewed"; no independent
+  review of such a PROCEED has been commissioned and none is fabricated here.
+- C4 is only partially met: the Executive order is signed but **inert**, with
+  `phase_gate_record: "PENDING — independent Judiciary officer-signed PROCEED ... no PROCEED is
+  fabricated here"`. `activation.json` keeps all four offices `enabled:false`, `not_before:0`.
+- The permit `permits/statistics-20261123.md` is also inert: its `effective_only_after` requires
+  enactment of the Rapid Full Institutional Activation Act, which is **not** in the current
+  authoritative `government/LAWS.md`.
+
+Attesting a PROCEED under these conditions would treat a byte-bound safety finding as valid for
+bytes it voids, and would convert a preparation/inert state into inferred activation authority.
+Absence of a clean byte match is negative evidence against a PROCEED claim, not proof of misconduct.
+
+**Re-attestation condition:** I will independently re-attest when (a) the exact §1 bytes are
+landed on canonical main, (b) `verify-landed` returns green for those exact bytes, and (c) an
+independent review of the attestation is commissioned. Economy may re-file a request with the
+then-current byte inventory; this decline is not a judgement on the trial's value.
